==English==

===Etymology===
The word psychoanalysis literally means "to release the soul from the ties that bind it". It comes from the Greek words [[ψυχή]] [[psycho-]] meaning "soul" and [[ανάλυσις]] meaning "a releasing", from [[αναλύω]] meaning "to undo".
From {{G.}} ''[[Psychoanalyse]]''

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{psychoanalysis}} a family of [[psychological]] theories and methods within the field of [[psychotherapy]] that work to find connections among patients' unconscious mental processes

